    - use_derived: call the implementation on a derived Type instance
      (deals in Tensors, not Variables); code on this dispatch path
      needs to wrap/unwrap tensors.

    - use_type: call the implementation on Type, because it is
      implemented concretely, and the functions it invokes will get
      dispatched back to VariableType (ensuring differentiability).
"""
def dispatch_strategy(declaration: dict[str, object]) -> str {
    if declaration['abstract'] or declaration['derivative'] is not None {
